:["CAD","Rhino","Grasshopper"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["│","URBAN SIMULATION"]},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"│"},{"text":"┌────────────┼────────────┐"},{"text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"text":"Mobility Climate Growth"},{"text":"Analysis Analysis Models"},{"text":"│ │ │"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["└────────────┼────────────┘","RESILIENT CITY DESIGN"]},{"type":"flow","items":["│","IMPLEMENTATION"]},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy","Development","Community"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong B.Arch graduate targeting Urban Design should be able to take an urban site through:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Urban Site","Site & Context Analysis","GIS Mapping","Urban Opportunities / Constraints","Urban Design Framework","Land-Use Strategy","Movement & Mobility","Street Network","Public Realm","Built Form & Density","Landscape / Green Infrastructure","3D / Parametric Visualisation","Phasing & Implementation"]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should ideally graduate with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong architectural design"},{"text":"Urban design fundamentals"},{"text":"Site planning"},{"text":"Urban morphology"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"Rhino/Grasshopper"},{"text":"3D visualisation"},{"text":"Urban planning fundamentals"},{"text":"Transportation fundamentals"},{"text":"Public-realm design"},{"text":"Climate-responsive design"},{"text":"Urban analytics"},{"text":"Basic Python"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Strong presentation skills"},{"text":"3–5 urban design projects"},{"text":"At least one urban planning/design/GIS internship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Portfolio"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Urban Design Portfolio"},{"text":"│"},{"text":"├── Neighbourhood Design"},{"text":"├── Master Plan"},{"text":"├── Transit-Oriented Development"},{"text":"├── Urban Regeneration"},{"text":"├── Public Realm / Streetscape"},{"text":"├── GIS-Based Urban Analysis"},{"text":"├── Climate-Resilient District"},{"text":"├── Urban Growth Study"},{"text":"└── Parametric / Computational Urban Design"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["A strong portfolio should show analysis","design reasoning","urban strategy","visualisation","implementation, rather than only attractive renderings"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Arch → Architecture → Urban Designer is a natural transition from building-scale design to city-scale spatial design."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Architecture","Urban Design","GIS","Urban Planning","Mobility","Public Realm","Climate Resilience","Computational Design"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For the modern urban-design market, adding GIS, spatial analytics, parametric design and climate-responsive planning provides a stronger differentiator than relying solely on conventional architectural visualization."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal progression is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Junior Urban Designer","Urban Designer","Senior Urban Designer","Urban Design Lead / Associate","Urban Design Director / City-Scale Design Strategist"]}]}]}